WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:16.590
Memorial Day in Israel is a day

00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:20.610
when people across the country
gather and remember those

00:00:20.610 --> 00:00:25.023
who were killed in the
military, typically in conflict.

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:36.540
Ludmila Rozhkov's son German Rozhkov

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:40.203
was killed in March of 2002.

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:47.070
When someone is killed in the army,

00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:51.090
a delegation is given the
very solemn and difficult task

00:00:51.090 --> 00:00:55.023
of going to the family and
telling them what has happened.

00:00:58.020 --> 00:01:00.330
They arrived at Ludmila's apartment,

00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:02.730
and she tried to block the door

00:01:02.730 --> 00:01:05.790
in the hope of blocking the truth.

00:01:05.790 --> 00:01:09.690
She was just beside herself with grief.

00:01:09.690 --> 00:01:11.287
And at a certain point, she said,

00:01:11.287 --> 00:01:14.697
"we must get German's sperm."

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:04.890
In Israel there is a growing practice

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:07.860
of post-mortem sperm retrieval,

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:12.000
in which, if a man dies in the military,

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:17.000
his family can ask the
military to retrieve sperm

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:22.520
from his corpse and to freeze
it to create a future child.

00:02:26.430 --> 00:02:30.720
The sperm in his testicles
continue to survive

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:35.313
for certainly 24 hours and,
indeed, possibly up to 72.

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:42.090
A skilled doctor can remove
sperm cells from his testicle

00:02:42.090 --> 00:02:46.530
and put them on ice, and it
can then sit for decades.

00:02:46.530 --> 00:02:50.043
And through in vitro
fertilization create a child.

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:56.550
It is banned in a number of
countries, but in Israel,

00:02:56.550 --> 00:03:00.780
which has an enormous embrace of pro natal

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:02.580
and fertility policies

00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:04.920
in order to build a strong population,

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:07.743
it is in fact, increasingly common.

00:03:10.110 --> 00:03:14.940
People who die in car accidents,
of cancer and so forth,

00:03:14.940 --> 00:03:17.430
their families have asked to use it.

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:19.650
We're not talking about huge numbers

00:03:19.650 --> 00:03:24.330
but in Israel the focus
right now is on young men

00:03:24.330 --> 00:03:26.193
who die in the military.

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:39.450
Sperm extraction is actually something

00:03:39.450 --> 00:03:42.993
that we've been doing for
as long as I remember.

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:51.483
But in the last years, it
became more and more frequent.

00:03:54.810 --> 00:03:58.920
I'm on call 24/7, and
sometimes I get a phone call

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:00.270
in the middle of the night.

00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:04.920
I watch TV and I see some breaking news

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:09.150
of some terrorist attack
in Tel Aviv or nearby.

00:04:09.150 --> 00:04:13.173
I tell myself, okay, sure
enough they will call me.

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:21.300
These relatives are in deep grief.

00:04:21.300 --> 00:04:26.130
They've just been notified that
their loved one was killed.

00:04:26.130 --> 00:04:31.130
Within a few hours, they can
get an approval from a judge

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:35.103
for us to perform this procedure.

00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:38.029
There is like a glimpse of hope

00:04:38.029 --> 00:04:40.083
and maybe a little bit of light.

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:49.530
There is a lot of responsibility
because you are helping

00:04:49.530 --> 00:04:54.513
to create a child who is
an orphan to begin with.

00:04:59.430 --> 00:05:03.090
Post-mortem sperm retrieval
has been more common

00:05:03.090 --> 00:05:05.460
when the man is married,

00:05:05.460 --> 00:05:09.060
but really what is so striking
about the situation in Israel

00:05:09.060 --> 00:05:12.690
is many people feel, "I
want to be a grandparent.

00:05:12.690 --> 00:05:15.720
This is an important stage
of life that I deserve.

00:05:15.720 --> 00:05:18.870
And if the state has
asked my son for service

00:05:18.870 --> 00:05:20.670
and he dies in that service,

00:05:20.670 --> 00:05:25.497
it owes me this help in
becoming a grandparent."

00:05:38.430 --> 00:05:42.870
It is now relatively common,
should a young man die

00:05:42.870 --> 00:05:45.630
in the military, for
the parents to be aware

00:05:45.630 --> 00:05:46.980
that they can ask for this.

00:05:46.980 --> 00:05:50.430
And then the military
will pay for the procedure

00:05:50.430 --> 00:05:54.780
as with Ludmila Rozhkov who
said, "I have lost my only son.

00:05:54.780 --> 00:05:56.520
I want a grandchild."

00:05:56.520 --> 00:05:59.013
And the court acknowledged
and agreed to that.

00:06:01.380 --> 00:06:04.290
In many ways, Ludmila was a pioneer

00:06:04.290 --> 00:06:06.870
who brought this to Israel.

00:06:06.870 --> 00:06:09.360
And interestingly, she's
not a native-born Israeli.

00:06:09.360 --> 00:06:10.787
She comes from Crimea.

00:09:23.127 --> 00:09:28.127
Ludmila took a long time
to decide how to proceed.

00:09:28.560 --> 00:09:31.140
It was about a dozen years after.

00:09:31.140 --> 00:09:34.440
And then it took four
years of a court battle

00:09:34.440 --> 00:09:37.680
for them to get permission
to use the sperm,

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:42.680
and the judge that they faced
quoted from the Hebrew Bible

00:09:43.110 --> 00:09:46.800
saying "pru u'rvu", "be
fruitful and multiply"

00:09:46.800 --> 00:09:50.730
but complications arose
in the court cases,

00:09:50.730 --> 00:09:55.730
because of the question of who
is in charge of this sperm.

00:09:56.160 --> 00:09:57.390
This is not the same thing

00:09:57.390 --> 00:09:59.550
as giving your kidney or your eye.

00:09:59.550 --> 00:10:02.193
This is creating another human being.

00:10:04.560 --> 00:10:08.700
The Supreme Court made a
ruling based not on the Bible

00:10:08.700 --> 00:10:13.140
but on what case law existed,
a decision which said

00:10:13.140 --> 00:10:16.020
there is no such thing as
a right to grandparenthood.

00:10:16.020 --> 00:10:21.020
We cannot grant this sperm to
someone other than the widow,

00:10:21.270 --> 00:10:24.300
and essentially sent a
message to the Knesset,

00:10:24.300 --> 00:10:25.890
to the parliament that said,

00:10:25.890 --> 00:10:28.713
if you want this thing to
move forward, we need a law.

00:10:33.630 --> 00:10:35.910
There are people creating a law,

00:10:35.910 --> 00:10:38.220
which will ask every young man,

00:10:38.220 --> 00:10:42.570
when he is inducted into the
military at the age of 18,

00:10:42.570 --> 00:10:46.290
whether he has something he
would like done with his sperm,

00:10:46.290 --> 00:10:48.070
should he die in uniform.

00:12:29.403 --> 00:12:32.493
There is an incredible focus

00:12:32.493 --> 00:12:35.310
on the family in Israel
and on having babies.

00:12:35.310 --> 00:12:40.310
So Israel has, from the very
beginning, viewed its role

00:12:41.220 --> 00:12:44.400
as a place to rebuild
the Jewish nation. Why?

00:12:44.400 --> 00:12:46.800
It comes, of course, just a few years

00:12:46.800 --> 00:12:48.360
after the Nazi Holocaust,

00:12:48.360 --> 00:12:51.060
in which 6 million Jews were slaughtered.

00:12:51.060 --> 00:12:54.570
So even though there's a fairly
heavy religious component

00:12:54.570 --> 00:12:58.380
in Israel, the fact is
there is a secular drive

00:12:58.380 --> 00:13:01.470
to have children in a
way that is incomparable

00:13:01.470 --> 00:13:03.633
in the rest of the wealthy world.

00:13:10.170 --> 00:13:15.170
We combine this with the
exceptional place of the military

00:13:15.420 --> 00:13:19.800
in Israeli society, where
essentially everyone puts in

00:13:19.800 --> 00:13:22.890
for boys three years for
girls a little under two years

00:13:22.890 --> 00:13:24.720
of military service.

00:13:24.720 --> 00:13:28.530
So everyone is linked to this institution.

00:13:28.530 --> 00:13:32.670
And when someone dies serving his country,

00:13:32.670 --> 00:13:37.410
the desire to honor that
person is also very pronounced.

00:13:37.410 --> 00:13:40.050
And so parents go onto Facebook

00:13:40.050 --> 00:13:42.727
or they get interviewed on
television and they say,

00:13:42.727 --> 00:13:45.900
"My son died in the
service of this country,

00:13:45.900 --> 00:13:50.340
and we're looking for a woman
to bear and raise his child."

00:13:50.340 --> 00:13:53.010
And what is remarkable is that hundreds,

00:13:53.010 --> 00:13:56.880
indeed thousands of
women raise their hands

00:13:56.880 --> 00:13:59.447
and volunteer to be that mother.

00:14:48.110 --> 00:14:51.720
Baruch Ben Ygal has been very involved

00:14:51.720 --> 00:14:53.670
with the Zvi Hauser law and others,

00:14:53.670 --> 00:14:57.427
because since the Supreme Court said,

00:14:57.427 --> 00:14:59.640
"We need to really have evidence

00:14:59.640 --> 00:15:03.000
that this young man wanted children,"

00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:05.970
he said, "I want to put all
my energy into creating a law

00:15:05.970 --> 00:15:08.470
instead of trying to go
through the court system."

00:15:09.450 --> 00:15:11.700
Although he said, "I am certain

00:15:11.700 --> 00:15:15.180
that he very much wanted to be a father."

00:15:15.180 --> 00:15:20.180
And he said to me, he has a
book of 5,000 names of women

00:15:20.910 --> 00:15:24.297
who want to be the mother
of his future grandchild.

00:17:31.270 --> 00:17:36.150
Broadly, Israel very much
embraces this process,

00:17:36.150 --> 00:17:38.013
but there are dissenters.

00:17:42.390 --> 00:17:45.630
There are deep worries, ethical and legal.

00:17:45.630 --> 00:17:47.820
People are saying, "I don't understand

00:17:47.820 --> 00:17:50.010
why would you do this on purpose?

00:17:50.010 --> 00:17:51.600
You are condemning this child

00:17:51.600 --> 00:17:53.910
to being a kind of living monument

00:17:53.910 --> 00:17:56.460
as opposed to having a
relatively normal life.

00:17:56.460 --> 00:17:57.957
Life is hard enough."

00:18:01.680 --> 00:18:06.190
So Baruch is very involved
in lobbying for this law

00:18:07.200 --> 00:18:09.750
and he is politically savvy and connected.

00:18:09.750 --> 00:18:12.780
So he's used those
connections for this cause.

00:18:12.780 --> 00:18:13.800
But he's not alone.

00:18:13.800 --> 00:18:18.800
There is a nonprofit
organization advocating for this

00:18:18.930 --> 00:18:20.940
in getting everybody on board.

00:18:20.940 --> 00:18:23.580
There obviously is hesitation
of the defense ministry

00:18:23.580 --> 00:18:26.790
and others to institutionalize
something like this,

00:18:26.790 --> 00:18:30.847
but it looks like it has the
wind at its back right now.

00:20:04.860 --> 00:20:09.390
So, when you first hear
about this procedure,

00:20:09.390 --> 00:20:12.813
it's hard not to feel a
little bit freaked out.

00:20:16.410 --> 00:20:18.840
At the same time, when
you meet these families

00:20:18.840 --> 00:20:23.040
and the fervor and love that
they bring to this fight,

00:20:23.040 --> 00:20:25.470
you melt, because you see

00:20:25.470 --> 00:20:28.860
that what is it that
drives us in life is love.

00:20:28.860 --> 00:20:33.630
And these people are engaged
in a fight for familial love.

00:20:33.630 --> 00:20:36.213
And that's a very powerful force.

